{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrxzCHTwn1PfGEhLamD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Line.is_parallel`, `is_perpendicular`, `smallest_angle_between` and `angle_between` now raise `TypeError('Must pass only LinearEntity objects')` when either argument isn't a `LinearEntity`.\n\nThe cause was that each of the four methods checked `not isinstance(l1, ...) and not isinstance(l2, ...)`. That only raised when both arguments were invalid, so a `Line` plus a `Point` got through and hit the `AttributeError`. I changed the `and` to `or` in all four checks in `sympy/geometry/line.py`.\n\nThe existing tests in `sympy/geometry/tests/test_line.py` pass (36 passed). I didn't re-run the exact example from the issue or add a test for the new behaviour."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":19614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":381},"output_tokens":255,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"513cc63e-2ef8-4106-b7d4-ef0dad5de19a","uuid":"88b8714a-82bb-461c-9552-e5dafaacf934","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:10:53.978Z","request_id":"req_011ChLrxz4qmvSxPFPiSMC6a"}
